[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518595559","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2518595559","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2518595559,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WHrfn","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T21:26:56Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T21:58:56Z","body":"I have made a simple benchmark (with auto lane-switching to the single-char string function disabled temporarily):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\tString s = \"Who is Frederic?Who is Frederic?Who is Frederic?\";\r\n\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 1000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tString s1 = s.replace(\"e\", \"b\");\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n\tt0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 1000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tString s1 = s.replace('e', 'b');\r\n\t}\r\n\tt1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n\tt0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 1000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tString s1 = s.replace(\"#\", \"b\");\r\n\t}\r\n\tt1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n\tt0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 1000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tString s1 = s.replace('#', 'b');\r\n\t}\r\n\tt1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis prints \r\n```\r\n253us\r\n84us\r\n24us\r\n18us\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, just very roughly, the single-char implementation can be:\r\n- About **3x as fast** when some characters are replaced (i.e. a copy is made).\r\n- About **1.3x as fast** when no characters are replaced (i.e. no copy is made).\r\n\r\n### contains\r\nA similar test for `contains`:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\tString s = \"Who is Frederic?Who is Frederic?Who is Frederic?\";\r\n\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tint x = s.contains(\"e\");\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n\tt0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100000; i ++) {\r\n\t\tint x = s.contains('e');\r\n\t}\r\n\tt1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"us\\n\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nprints\r\n\r\n```\r\n622us\r\n501us\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, it also benefits from single-char optimization, though not as much (`1.24x`). But at the same time, its optimization was already implemented, so I'm only contributing by relaying a few calls to it instead of the `char *` based variant.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518595559/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520801037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2520801037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2520801037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WQF8N","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T16:13:32Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T16:17:36Z","body":"This is a duplicate of (which is more complete and uses more distinguishable syntax):\r\n* #92475 \r\n\r\nBut the use of `replace` on `CowData` does make sense","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/25208