,"id":2520868860,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WQWf8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T16:38:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T16:38:40Z","body":"I think separating this or removing the duplicate parts would be good, and I'd say focusing on the `contains` part (and naming it `contains_char` for completeness, and ability to bind to scripting)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520868860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520890087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2520890087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2520890087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WQbrn","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T16:43:54Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T16:43:54Z","body":"> I think separating this or removing the duplicate parts would be good, and I'd say focusing on the `contains` part (and naming it `contains_char` for completeness, and ability to bind to scripting)\r\n\r\nSounds good to me! Then I will remove the duplicate parts from this PR and continue commenting on yours.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520890087/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520891262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2520891262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2520891262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WQb9-","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T16:44:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T16:44:24Z","body":"Thank you, will investigate the alternative solutions and see what we can make!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2520891262/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525312951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2525312951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2525312951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhTe3","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T21:16:04Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T21:26:55Z","body":"> I'd much rather see a String::contains(const char_t), or equivalent overload. So future developers can't make the mistake. \r\n\r\nI had it as an `String::contains` overload first, but I was requested above to rename it to `contains_char` because similar single-char functions are appended with `_char`. I believe the main reason is that it is easier to bind to scripting languages this way?\r\n\r\n> It also will make the change local to ustring.cpp/h\r\n\r\nHow would that be possible? Callers that currently call with `contains(char *)` will have to be adjusted to use the single-char function with either the `contains` name and the `contains_char` name. The only way to make it consistently select the single-char implementation at compile time would be to expose the `strlen(x) == 1` check in the header file, which I'm not sure if it is a good idea to do for every single function. Or idk, maybe it is - it would bloat the header file somewhat, requiring inlining by String callers, but it's a fairly simple check.\r\n\r\n> , or a (const char[2]) overload, I guess. perhaps both?\r\n\r\nI experimented with this earlier, but this logic would fail for `contains({ 'a', 'b' })` which is not appended with `NULL`. Yeah, it's a bit annoying. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525312951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525316018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2525316018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2525316018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhUOy","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T21:28:45Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T21:28:45Z","body":"> > I'd much rather see a String::contains(const char_t), or equivalent overload. So future developers can't make the mistake.\r\n> \r\n> I had it as an `String::contains` overload first, but I was requested above to rename it to `contains_char` because similar single-char functions are appended with `_char`. I believe the main reason is that it is easier to bind to scripting languages this way?\r\n\r\nThe speed improvements of contains_char would have to be massive for it to matter in gdscript, but perhaps I'm being too pessimistic :P \r\n\r\n> > It also will make the change local to ustring.cpp/h\r\n> \r\n> How would that be possible? Callers that currently call with `contains(char *)` will have to be adjusted to use the single-char function with either the `contains` name and the `contains_char` name. The only way to make it consistently select the single-char implementation at compile time would be to expose the `strlen(x) == 1` check in the header file, which I'm not sure if it is a good idea to do for every single function.\r\n>\r\n\r\nIf we do a const char[2] overload, we can just assume size=1, right? \r\n\r\n> > , or a (const char[2]) overload, I guess. perhaps both?\r\n> \r\n> I experimented with this earlier, but this logic would fail for `contains({ 'a', 'b' })` which is not appended with `NULL`. Yeah, it's a bit annoying.\r\n\r\nWouldn't that fail now also? If there's no null it'd just crash now, no? as in, that is already an error?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525316018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525320702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2525320702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2525320702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhVX-","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T21:48:50Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T21:50:22Z","body":"> The speed improvements of contains_char would have to be massive for it to matter in gdscript, but perhaps I'm being too pessimistic :P\r\n\r\nGDScript may not benefit, but C# and GDExtension also use the scripting interface (though I also don't know what that has to do with the c++ exposed name).\r\n\r\n> If we do a const char[2] overload, we can just assume size=1, right?\r\n> \r\n> > > , or a (const char[2]) overload, I guess. perhaps both?\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > I experimented with this earlier, but this logic would fail for `contains({ 'a', 'b' })` which is not appended with `NULL`. Yeah, it's a bit annoying.\r\n> \r\n> Wouldn't that fail now also? If there's no null it'd just crash now, no? as in, that is already an error?\r\n\r\nThis turns out to be surprisingly difficult to answer, lol.\r\n\r\nHere's a test I just ran to answer this question:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nstatic const char s[] = { 'a', 'b' };\r\n\r\ntemplate <size_t l>\r\nsize_t test(const char (&s)[l]) {\r\n\treturn l;\r\n}\r\n\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) size_t test2(const char *s) {\r\n\treturn strlen(s);\r\n}\r\n\r\nint main()\r\n{\r\n\tstd::cout << strlen(s) << std::endl;\r\n\tstd::cout << test(s) << std::endl;\r\n\tstd::cout << test2(s) << std::endl;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt prints\r\n```\r\n2\r\n2\r\n24\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat's right, `clang` cheats with its strlen implementation, assuming a `NULL` terminator at compile time when it should probably complain instead.\r\n\r\nIn any case, calling `String.contains({ 'a', 'b' })` would yield unexpected behavior. If evaluated at compile time, it would return `String.contains(`a`)`. If evaluated at runtime, it might even `SIGSEV`. I guess it would be fair to document the behavior of this function. This is one of the reasons I used `strlen` instead of `len` in #99806 even for the arrays known at compile time - it failed unit tests otherwise.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525320702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525321248","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2525321248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2525321248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhVgg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T21:51:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T21:51:27Z","body":"> If we can't get it merged with an overload lets just keep it like this. Maybe we can do a pass over all of the _char functions and just remove them in one fell swoop eventually.\r\n\r\nThat's fair; for the record, I also think a `contains` overload without a `_char` suffix is more appropriate. But it's something we could address later, it's not a dealbreaker.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525321248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525322845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2525322845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2525322845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WhV5d","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T21:59:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T21:59:24Z","body":"@Ivorforce surely  calling `strlen()` on a char array without a null terminator is already UB. I think you're just digging into how surprising the UB is. :P `strlen({'a', 'b'});` might kill your cat and you don't get to complain about it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2525322845/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":2,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2529393407","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100024#issuecomment-2529393407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100024","id":2529393407,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ww3r_","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-09T20:36:54Z","updated_at":"2024-12-09T20:36:54Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2529393407/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]